    <properties>
        <project.build.sourceEncoding>UTF-8</project.build.sourceEncoding>
        <codemirror.version>4.10</codemirror.version>
        <handlebars.version>4.7.7</handlebars.version>
        <!--
            Applies ONLY to the tgz:npm artifacts copied by copy-commons-npm-tarballs below.
            The commons.ui:user:zip:www dependency stays at the version the imported BOM chain
            manages (3.1.2): that BOM is scope=import, so its properties interpolate inside the
            BOM and this one cannot reach it. The build therefore composes AMD/www sources at
            3.2.0-SNAPSHOT over vendor libraries pinned at 3.1.2, and nothing checks the two
            agree - a vendor bump in commons 3.2 will not reach AM. Task 3.10 records the
            coupling, 3.12 removes the pin.

            PREREQUISITE: no released commons carries a tgz:npm artifact, so these resolve from
            ~/.m2 only. Build them first, from the sibling commons checkout on branch
            features/ui-migration:
                mvn install -f ui/pom.xml
            Without that this module fails at `initialize` with "Could not find artifact
            org.openidentityplatform.commons.ui:commons:tgz:npm:3.2.0-SNAPSHOT".

            AND BUILD THIS MODULE FROM ../ (openam-ui), NOT FROM HERE. The ~58 commons.ui.libs
            artifacts are published to no repository; they exist only because
            maven-external-dependency-plugin fetches them from CDNs, and that plugin is
            inherited=false on the openam-ui aggregator with install-external bound to
            process-resources. A standalone build here never runs it and dies resolving
            selectize-non-standalone, text, sifter, ... from Central. Use:
                mvn -DskipTests package        (from openam-ui)
            NEVER `mvn clean` on openam-ui, and never `mvn ... -am` from the OpenAM root:
            clean-external DELETES those artifacts from ~/.m2 and nothing can restore them but
            a CDN round trip. Use `rm -rf target` instead.
        -->
        <commons.ui.version>3.2.0-SNAPSHOT</commons.ui.version>
        <font-awesome.version>4.5.0</font-awesome.version>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
